      en: "Spijkenisse, in South Holland, on the island of Voorne-Putten, has about 72,000 inhabitants. It became a municipality in 1960 and grew as a Rotterdam suburb post-WWII. Modern architecture includes De Terp shopping center and Schouwburg de Stoep theatre. The marina serves leisure boating. The city is connected to Rotterdam by metro. Economy relies on retail, services, and local industry. Spijkenisse offers green spaces and parks, and the nearby Oude Maas river for recreation.",
