      en: "Genemuiden is a city in Overijssel, Netherlands, at the confluence of the Zwartewater and the Zwarte Meer. Chartered in 1275, it grew as a fishing and shipbuilding hub. In the 20th century, the carpet industry became dominant. The 15th-century Grote Kerk is a notable landmark. Population is about 10,000. The city has a small marina and borders the Weerribben-Wieden National Park, a vast peat bog area. Today, manufacturing remains important, alongside services. Genemuiden also hosts an annual flower parade.",
