      en: "Hippolytushoef is the main town of the former island of Wieringen in North Holland, Netherlands. After the Afsluitdijk was completed in 1932, Wieringen became part of the mainland. The town is named after Saint Hippolytus. The Gothic Grote Kerk dates from the 15th century. Hippolytushoef lies along the Wadden Sea, a UNESCO World Heritage site. The economy relies on agriculture (arable farming and livestock) and tourism. The population is around 4,500. The marina hosts recreational boats, and the area is popular for mudflat hiking.",
